Cell[TextData[{
 "Create a number of Neural Networks and state how good the best one is \
(justify your answer).\n",
 StyleBox["Answer:\n",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.840607725384644*^9, 3.840607760872209*^9}, {
   3.8406078022778606`*^9, 3.8406078102046776`*^9}, {3.8406106963508224`*^9, 
   3.8406107088405824`*^9}, {3.8406109923753786`*^9, 3.840611013098338*^9}, {
   3.8406110693175955`*^9, 3.8406111194349594`*^9}, {3.840619531338698*^9, 
   3.8406196000348096`*^9}, {3.840620019754721*^9, 3.8406200231767826`*^9}, {
   3.840620153516815*^9, 3.8406201535701885`*^9}, {3.84062096077177*^9, 
   3.840620982907363*^9}, {3.840621944987389*^9, 3.8406219678998766`*^9}, {
   3.840622303353545*^9, 3.8406223553882604`*^9}, 3.840622556881044*^9, {
   3.8406248249090548`*^9, 3.8406248255704236`*^9}, 3.8406252575298567`*^9, {
   3.840625317360176*^9, 3.8406253189368353`*^9}, {3.8406254066434803`*^9, 
   3.840625409575193*^9}, {3.8426945668509054`*^9, 3.842694576196881*^9}, {
   3.9036814018732476`*^9, 3.9036814558905735`*^9}, {3.9036815438739133`*^9, 
   3.9036815702872095`*^9}, 4.003680581938758*^9, {4.003680878155481*^9, 
   4.0036808798604283`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3ccfa633-1afe-4f6a-98cc-\
d8c53249db40"],

Cell["\<\
Before we begin training our models, we want to have test data to see how \
well our neural network is doing against data it has not seen yet

Best Neural Network -> NN 5. We choose NN5 as the best neural network for our \
problem, as this neural network performed the best against the test data with \
66.67% and we managed to eliminate the constant issue of overfitting

Overview of neural networks
\[LineSeparator]- NN1: Without an idea of how we should structure our neural \
networks for this data, we went overboard with the amount of neurons leading \
to a poorly performing overfit model. We can see this model is overfit, as  \
the training accuracy (100) and testing accuracy (42) is extremely lob sided \
towards the training accuracy
We establish the model with 12 inputs (encoded teams = 8 + home and away \
shots + home and away shots on target),  
A connected layer with 64 neurons, 
The ReLU or Ramp activation function introducing non-linearity turning \
negative values to 0 and letting positive values through,  
Convert the values into a smoother range between 0 and 1
A connected layer that maps to our 3 outputs\[LineSeparator]And softmax that \
convert the outputs into values that add up to 100%

- NN2: For this neural network we tried to eliminate the overfitting issue, \
but if anything we ended up underfitting on this model. The structure was the \
same as the previous neural network, except we altered the amount of neurons \
and reduced down to one layer. We can see this nn is underfitting as the \
training and test accuracy is low.

- NN3: On this nn we tried to strike a healthy medium between the \
underfitting and overfitting models. With two layers. But we could not avoid \
the issue with overfitting.

(*Reference - \
https://reference.wolfram.com/language/tutorial/NeuralNetworksRegularization.\
html*)
- NN4 : At this point, we tried normalisation using dropout to try avoid the \
constant issue of overfitting, however after much trial and error (with \
neurons, layers and activation functions) we decided dropout does not work to \
avoid overfitting for this data. Also this led to inconsistencies with \
results as each run would choose different neurons to dropout

(*Reference - \
https://reference.wolfram.com/language/tutorial/NeuralNetworksRegularization.\
html*)
- NN5 : We still wanted to eliminate (at least try to) overfitting, so we \
tried the normalisation technique weight decay. This applies a penalty to the \
nn\[CloseCurlyQuote]s loss function based on the size of the weights. After \
messing around with the L2Regularization value, we landed on 0.04, which \
yielded the best results (in terms of test data) so far.
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8406077657661633`*^9, 3.8406077988842287`*^9}, {
  3.8406248407328467`*^9, 3.8406248433065586`*^9}, {4.0036698179283805`*^9, 
  4.0036700743789797`*^9}, {4.0036701073955097`*^9, 4.0036702379455233`*^9}, {
  4.0036808837396746`*^9, 4.003680919498017*^9}, {4.0036810961461115`*^9, 
  4.0036811338410816`*^9}, {4.003681201631735*^9, 4.0036812290991945`*^9}, {
  4.0036813132851024`*^9, 4.0036815966794424`*^9}, {4.003681796037496*^9, 
  4.003681853916927*^9}, {4.0036819373526044`*^9, 4.0036819414360757`*^9}, {
  4.0036823287026596`*^9, 4.0036823352387533`*^9}, {4.0036823691708937`*^9, 
  4.0036824196573343`*^9}, {4.00368248519573*^9, 4.0036825080863843`*^9}, {
  4.0036825550366225`*^9, 4.0036826704145346`*^9}, {4.0036829601477323`*^9, 
  4.0036829739825687`*^9}, {4.0038372908172064`*^9, 
  4.003837382091177*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b1fb2533-13f4-42a4-a1f0-\
c00bf6fea910"],

